      "id": 20,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "HTTP request rate, latency and 5xx by route",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus-mail"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### signal not exported yet\n\nThe panels this row would hold cannot be built today. The cluster Prometheus (`prometheus-mail`) scrapes only these jobs: `kepler`, `kube-state-metrics`, `node-bumble`, `node-honey`, `node-relay`, `node-sting`, `nut-exporter`, `prometheus`, `rspamd`. No metric name below exists in any datasource on this Grafana; none has been invented here.\n\n| Wanted signal | Metric that would carry it | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ingress request rate by route | `nginx_ingress_controller_requests` | **absent** \u2014 the `ingress-nginx` namespace runs, but its controller metrics are not scraped |\n| p50 / p95 request latency | `nginx_ingress_controller_request_duration_seconds_bucket` | **absent** |\n| 5xx by route | `nginx_ingress_controller_requests{status=~\"5..\"}` | **absent** |\n| Cloudflare Tunnel health | `cloudflared_tunnel_*` | **absent** \u2014 the `cloudflared` namespace runs but exports no metrics to this Prometheus |\n| Cloudflare Access denials | Cloudflare Logpush / GraphQL analytics | **absent** \u2014 no Cloudflare datasource is configured on this Grafana |\n| Application request metrics | app `/metrics` on the SvelteKit adapter-node pod | **absent** \u2014 the workload exposes `/health` only, and is not scraped |\n\nKube-state-metrics does export `kube_ingress_info`, `kube_ingress_path` and `kube_ingress_tls`, but those describe Ingress *objects*, not traffic. GFTB public traffic reaches the pod through the `cloudflared` tunnel namespace (see the NetworkPolicy in `k8s/web/greatfallstoolbus-org-production/`), not through an in-cluster ingress controller, so an ingress-controller scrape would not capture GFTB traffic even if it were enabled.\n\n**To light these panels up**, an operator-gated change would have to add a request-metrics source on the GFTB serving path and a matching scrape job. That is a separate ticket: this dashboard set deliberately ships the gap visible rather than inventing metric names.\n\nPrivacy note: per `meta/spec/observability-shape-2026-06-05.md`, the launch site ships zero analytics and the edge must drop client IPs. Any future request-rate panel must be route-shaped and IP-free."
      }
    }
